item.description:
Democrats retook both the House and Senate after romping through multiple deep-red states in a historic midterm election. Is this a product of President Donald Trump’s historic unpopularity, or a more fundamental reshaping of our politics? We take stock of the map and how Democrats could approach being in the majority for the final two years of Trump’s term.&nbsp;

---&nbsp;

Guest: David Chalian, CNN Washington Bureau Chief/Political Director&nbsp;

Host: David Rind&nbsp;

Producer: Paola Ortiz&nbsp;

Showrunner: Felicia Patinkin&nbsp;
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices

